.* SETUP: the task menu for customizing the system.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='SETUP'.
:IMPORT NAME=CHGUSRPRF PNLGRP=QHSYCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKSYSVAL PNLGRP=QHSVCMD.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/MENUKEYS' NAME=MENUKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.F1=Help
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION='CMD CALL QCMD'.F9=Command line
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=SETUP HELP=HLPSETUP KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.Customize Your System, Users, and Devices
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.To select an option, type its number below and press Enter:
:MENUI HELP=WRKSYSVAL OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD WRKSYSVAL'.Change system options
:MENUI HELP='SETUP/OPT2' OPTION=2 ACTION='MENU CLEANUP'.Cleanup tasks
:MENUI HELP='SETUP/OPT3' OPTION=3 ACTION='MENU POWER'.Power on and off tasks
:MENUI HELP='SETUP/OPT4' OPTION=4 ACTION='MENU DISKTASKS'.Disk space tasks
:MENUI HELP='SETUP/OPT5' OPTION=5 ACTION='MENU BACKUP'.Backup tasks
:MENUI HELP=CHGUSRPRF OPTION=11 ACTION='CMD ?CHGUSRPRF USRPRF(QSECOFR)'.Change passwords for IBM-supplied users
:MENUI HELP='SETUP/OPT20' OPTION=20 ACTION='MENU CMNCFG'.Communications configuration tasks
:EMENU.
:BOTINST.Type a menu option below
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPSETUP.Customize Your System, Users, and Devices - Help
:P.Setting the system up the way this site wants it: options, cleanup,
power, backup and the passwords of the shipped profiles.
:P.Type an option number and press Enter. F9 opens a command line, F3
leaves the menu and F12 returns to the one before it.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F1=Help
:PD.Shows help for where the cursor is.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F9=Command line
:PD.Shows a command line to run a command from.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SETUP/OPT2'.Cleanup tasks
:P.Option 2. Shows menu CLEANUP&colon. Cleanup tasks.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SETUP/OPT3'.Power on and off tasks
:P.Option 3. Shows menu POWER&colon. Power on and off tasks.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SETUP/OPT4'.Disk space tasks
:P.Option 4. Shows menu DISKTASKS&colon. Disk space tasks.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SETUP/OPT5'.Backup tasks
:P.Option 5. Shows menu BACKUP&colon. Backup tasks.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SETUP/OPT20'.Communications configuration tasks
:P.Option 20. Shows menu CMNCFG&colon. Communications configuration
tasks.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
